Subject: [PATCH 5/6] WP-0.7, enforcement (cld-advisor's series 5, patch 5;
 built on a35fd4bce with the ten patches of series 4 and the first four of
 series 5 applied): A GATE READS THE COMMIT'S FILES, AND ONE IT CANNOT READ IT
 DOES NOT PASS OVER (Review 79, the second reader's row 24). Three places.
 ONE, the gate on the lists of hashed files. A tracked list that could not be
 read was left out, and with it every entry it holds: the gate then passed,
 having found nothing wrong among fewer. A tracked file that a list names and
 that could not be read was recorded as a file that is not there, which is the
 state an entry can be frozen in. Now a list under its usual name that cannot
 be read fails the gate, and a tracked file that cannot be read is in a state
 of its own, which fails it too. TWO, the gate on sentences of arrival. Where
 its folder is a git checkout and git would not list the tracked files, it
 walked the disk in their place and read whatever stood there; and a page it
 could not read it passed over. Now it says that it cannot verify, and a page
 that cannot be read fails it by name. A folder that is no checkout is still
 walked: that is a test's small tree. THREE, the runner. A passing sentence
 that held the word skipped was printed as a gate that had read nothing. The
 gate on the generated pages says that it compared every page and left one
 check in part where the seats' branches are absent, and was printed so. A
 gate that read in part is now printed as a pass, with its whole sentence, so
 that what it left is said and is never a bare ok. One assertion of main's own
 test of that gate held the line to begin with SKIP; it now holds it to begin
 with PASS and to carry the sentence, with a dated note. LEFT AS IT IS, and
 why: where a list names no tracked file the gate looks on the disk to name
 the state, absent or not tracked. Both are one state for the gate, which
 main's own test holds, so the answer does not depend on the disk. And a file
 under another name that cannot be read may be no list at all, and is passed
 over as before. The lock: five tests added to
 tests/test_a_gate_reads_all_it_is_about.py. On the commit before, all five
 fail: the hash gate passes over a list it cannot read, and reads a tracked
 file it cannot read as not there; the arrival gate answers from an untracked
 draft, and passes over a page it cannot read; the runner prints SKIP. Tested
 against planted errors, 5 of 5; computed once. 0 of 19.

